  "family": "Salicaceae",
  "memo": "The Pacific willow grows throughout western California and the Sierra Nevada foothills and north to Alaska. It is distinguishable from other willows by the warty glands present where the leafstalk meets the blade. It has an upright, asymmetric crown with a short, dark trunk and long branches bearing yellowish-brown twigs and yellowish-green leaves that are shiny on the upper surface and whitish below.",
