  "california_native": 1,
  "ethnobotanical_info": "The branches and twigs of &lt;em&gt;Salix lasiandra&lt;/em&gt; are used by Pacific Northwest Tribes for fishing weirs, bows, and hand drills. Most importantly, they are used to weave baskets. Medicinally, willow bark contains salicyclic acid used to treat fevers and headaches, reduce inflammation, and relieve pain. Aspirin is a commonly used synthetic derivative of this compound. Its leaves and branches are used as a disinfectant.&nbsp;",
